WEBVTT


00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:00.810
Oops.

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.620
I caught the tail of my shirt on
a single needle as I walked by.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:09.270
Luckily, the machine was secured and
didn't fall, but this needle needs to be

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.080
replaced.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:15.630
Get comfortable with replacing needles
on your machine, and you won't panic when

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:17.160
something like this happens.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:22.440
Now, if you have a replacement sponge
bar on hand, now might be a good time to

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.010
replace it.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:30.905
Get started replacing that needle by
pulling out your sponge bar just to the

00:00:30.905 --> 00:00:33.635
position of the bent or broken needle.

00:00:35.385 --> 00:00:40.185
Reach the other end and grab the opposite
end of the sponge bar to pull it out.

00:00:42.435 --> 00:00:46.785
Now notice how the needles pop up
when the sponge bar is removed.

00:00:47.445 --> 00:00:49.935
This will allow you to take
out that broken needle.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.000
Grab the butt of the needle
and pull it towards you.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:01:00.720
Lifting up on the back of the needle, push
it back and up and wiggle it a little bit,

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.120
and then pull the hook
end out of the slot.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:07.980
Now replace the needle
in the reverse order.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.930
Place the hook end in the slot.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.200
Pull it forward and drop
the back of the needle.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.030
End of the track and push back.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:26.560
Use your needle pusher to hold down the
needles and slide that sponge bar back

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.520
into place.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:28.780
Voila.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:29.590
You're all done.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:32.850
Thank you for watching.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.140
Please take a look at the growing
learning library at Knit it Now

